Findy - Lost & Found Management System

Findy is a smart, web-based platform designed to bridge the gap between people who have lost items and those who have found them. It utilizes Artificial Intelligence (AI) for image recognition to automatically match lost and found items, providing a seamless and secure recovery process.
![alt text](https://via.placeholder.com/1200x300?text=Findy+-+Reuniting+You+With+What+Matters)
<!-- Replace with actual screenshot if available -->
🚀 Features
🔍 AI-Powered Matching: Automatically compares images of found items against lost reports using TensorFlow (MobileNet).
👥 Multi-User Roles: Separate portals for Users, Organizations (e.g., Malls, Metro), Moderators, and Admins.
📱 Item Reporting: Easy-to-use forms to report Lost or Found items with image uploads and location tagging.
🗺️ Geolocation: Integration with Leaflet/Geoapify to pin exact locations where items were lost or found.
💬 Secure Chat (Help Desk): Private communication channel between finder and owner, unlocked only after a potential match is verified.
🔔 Smart Notifications: Email alerts for community broadcasts and match confirmations.
📊 Analytics Dashboard: Real-time stats and charts for Admins and Organizations to track recovery rates.
🛠️ Tech Stack
Frontend
React.js: Component-based UI library.
Material UI (MUI): Professional design system and components.
Recharts: Data visualization for dashboards.
Axios: HTTP client for API requests.
Backend
Node.js & Express.js: Server-side runtime and framework.
MongoDB & Mongoose: NoSQL database for flexible data storage.
JWT (JSON Web Tokens): Secure authentication.
Multer: Middleware for handling image uploads.
Nodemailer: Service for sending email notifications.
AI & Processing
TensorFlow.js: For running ML models on the server.
MobileNet: Pre-trained model for image feature extraction.
Sharp: High-performance image processing (resizing/formatting).
String-Similarity: For comparing text descriptions.
⚙️ Installation & Setup
Prerequisites
Node.js (v14 or higher)
MongoDB (Local or Atlas)
Python (Optional, if using the Python script fallback)
1. Clone the Repository
code
Bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/findy.git
cd findy
2. Backend Setup
Navigate to the server folder and install dependencies.
code
Bash
cd Server
npm install
Create a .env file in the Server directory:
code
Env
PORT=5001
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
JWT_SECRET=your_super_secret_key
EMAIL_USERNAME=your_email@gmail.com
EMAIL_PASSWORD=your_email_app_password
GEOAPIFY_API_KEY=your_geoapify_key
Start the Server:
code
Bash
npm start
# Server runs on http://localhost:5001
3. Frontend Setup
Open a new terminal, navigate to the client folder, and install dependencies.
code
Bash
cd Client
npm install
Start the React App:
code
Bash
npm start
# Client runs on http://localhost:3000
📂 Project Structure
code
Code
Findy/
├── Client/                 # React Frontend
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── components/     # UI Components (User, Org, Mod, Admin)
│   │   ├── Styles/         # CSS Files
│   │   ├── api/            # Axios instance
│   │   └── App.js          # Main Router
├── Server/                 # Node.js Backend
│   ├── controllers/        # Business Logic (Item, User, Chat)
│   ├── models/             # Mongoose Schemas
│   ├── routes/             # API Endpoints
│   ├── utils/              # Helpers (Email, AI)
│   └── index.js            # Entry Point
└── README.md               # Project Documentation
🧪 Testing

Manual Testing
Register two accounts: User A and User B.
User A reports a "Lost Item" (e.g., Black Wallet).
User B reports a "Found Item" with a similar image.
Check User A's email for a match notification.
Verify the match in the Help Desk and test the chat functionality.
Unit Testing
Run backend tests (if configured):
code
Bash
cd Server
npm test
